/*
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Ottilie contract test — inputs on the PRIVATE Azure Blob (az://), for Azure Batch / Seqera
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Same 2-sample / 4-chromosome test as `ottilie_test`, with every input an az:// path on
    the private `aletest` container. This is the profile a Seqera Launchpad entry should name.

    Usage:  tw launch <entry> -p docker,ottilie_test_az   (outdir supplied per run)
            nextflow run main.nf -profile ottilie_test_az,docker -c conf/azure_batch.config

    ⚠️ `outdir` is deliberately NOT set here. publishDir overwrites but never deletes, so a
    reused directory silently accumulates stale outputs from older pipeline versions and makes
    any comparison untrustworthy. Supply a fresh dated one per run — that is the single value
    the Launchpad's parameters box should still carry.

    WHY az:// AND NOT THE PUBLIC https PROFILE (`ottilie_test_ci`):
      - `snpeff_cache` is a *directory* param. Nextflow's http provider cannot list a directory,
        so ottilie_test_ci points it at a LOCAL dir that bin/test_ottilie_blob.sh untars before
        launching — a pre-launch step a Platform head job never performs. az:// stages
        directories natively, so no untar and no launcher coupling.
      - Inputs stay intra-region and private instead of crossing the public internet each run.

    ⚠️ THE WORK DIR MUST BE IN THE SAME CONTAINER (`aletest`) as these inputs whenever the run
    uses the Entra service principal: Nextflow mints ONE container-scoped SAS and reuses it for
    every blob URL, so a node cannot read another container even in the same storage account.
    See docs/dev-practices/azure_batch_execution.md §3.

    ⚠️ A LAUNCHPAD RUN CLONES FROM GITHUB, NOT FROM YOUR WORKING TREE. Edits to this file do not
    reach a Platform launch until they are committed AND pushed to the registered revision.

    Data layout, and how this 2-sample set differs from the 4-sample pilot:
    docs/benchmarking/ottilie_xenobiotic_ale/blob_layout.md
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
*/

// Container + versioned prefix. Override for a v2 prefix or a different account.
def az_base = System.getenv('OTTILIE_AZ_BASE') ?: 'az://aletest/ottilie/v1'

// Callers, joint-germline settings and snpeff_db are shared with every other ottilie profile.
includeConfig 'ottilie_common.config'

params {
    config_profile_name        = 'Ottilie Test Profile (private az:// blob)'
    config_profile_description = 'Minimal yeast ALE test from az://aletest — 2 samples, 4 chromosomes'

    // Input — samplesheet whose fastq_1/fastq_2 are az:// paths
    input                      = "${az_base}/samplesheet_test_az.csv"

    // Reference — the 4-chromosome SUBSET (_test), not the full genome
    fasta                      = "${az_base}/S288C_reference_test/S288C_R64_test.fa"
    genbank                    = "${az_base}/S288C_reference_test/S288C_R64_test.gb"
    chr_dir                    = "${az_base}/S288C_reference_test/chromosomes"

    // Annotation cache — a directory, staged straight from blob (the DB version is in the common config)
    snpeff_cache               = "${az_base}/S288C_reference_test/snpeff_cache"

    // Mutation report — the igv-reports dashboard. ON.
    // Pinned rather than inherited: it matches the nextflow.config default today, but a Platform
    // run should not silently change behaviour if that default ever moves. (Deliberately NOT in
    // ottilie_common.config — the local profiles leave it inherited, and the nf-test drives it
    // through its own `when` block.)
    generate_reports           = true

    // Gene-annotation track for the igv-reports dashboards.
    // ⚠️ Note the path: S288C_reference/, NOT the _test subset — this has always been the
    // full-genome gff3, and it is the one reference file the two datasets share.
    report_gff3                = "${az_base}/S288C_reference/S288C_R64.gff3"
}
